{"authored" [{"question" "q-330498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-2,4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨0,3,-5⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨1,-2,4⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨0,3,-5⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =⟨1,-2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨0,3,-5⟩ & =-26 \\\\ 3y-5z & =-26 \\\\ 3y-5z+26 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+y-5z+26=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3y+5z+26=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3y-5z+24=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3y-5z+26=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-330498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3y-5z-26=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=3i+4j-k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-2,3,-1⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨3,4,-1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨-2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,4,-1⟩ & =7 \\\\ 3x+4y-z & =7 \\\\ 3x+4y-z-7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5208ba3a6d61c1d854213da0bd411d1d488a847f908e755c4b38c9fe7efa72b" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.json" "file_sha256" "118742b33fefe44dd1f2d61224db83b6a930b4b464865d14cf06c0c7d7730350" "basis" 1571 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+4y-z-7=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042721/state.js